														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2587897">
									

<p>Thanks goes to Rimple, mf99k, Jack Ike, AidenEldritch, Overandover, and anyone else who looked at this while I was crybabying about it in chat this whole weekend. Feels good to finally get a major part of my List off of my List and onto the wiki.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Some&nbsp;author&nbsp;commentary</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide&nbsp;author&nbsp;commentary</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This is absolute, definitive MacCanon on how Alexei dies. All other adventures written about him are alt-universe stuff, or not in alignment with my intentions.</p>
<p>This story takes place in a continuity wherein <a href="/scp-2217">SCP-2217</a> forces the Foundation to go public and release all of its least-harmful wards in an effort to save face. There may be more stories about this motley crew, but I have none planned in the immediate future. I can elaborate on anyone's questions, but would prefer people to keep spoilers in collapsibles.</p>
<p>ETA that, for those of you wondering about the URL, this is meant to be a half-assed revival of the &quot;Future Foundation&quot; project that was started and then died about a year and a half ago.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide&nbsp;author&nbsp;commentary</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I hope you all enjoy it!</p>

